      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Intravascular Doppler assessment of coronary flow velocity has demonstrated the physiologic significance of intermediate stenoses and the success of coronary interventions. We describe a patient where Doppler evaluation confirmed the significance of an intermediate left circumflex ostial stenosis. We also describe the Doppler flow velocity characteristics after successful rotational atherectomy facilitated angioplasty."},
